Evaluator Note:
PC: painful & clicking of knees
HPC: thinks over done workout; weird tingling in toes and pain when running and clicking heard in knees;  ongoing for 2/52; no prev joint problems; plays ice hockey; fell on ice and had a big bruise; training for marathon; started about a month ago; usually a few mile runs; goes to gym a few times a week; not felt knees being unstable; usually starts after about 20 mins; has had to stop a few times during runs; affects both knees; right knee more so than left; no issues really with left; feels like there is fluid in knee; knee was swollen before which settled with ice; not painful at rest; no clicking if extending leg; only if running or working out; able to straighten knee; no locking; able to walk normally; able to fully straighten leg and flex it; prn ibuprofen; occasionally would smoke a joint to help with pain; no pain in other joints; notice ankle swelling in ankles; one off tingling in toes after run; in right foot only; no calf pain; no arch problems;
PMHX: far sighted had laser surgery; kidney issues;
MEDS: vit D, melatonin,

